If the input element is created dynamically and you do not have it in hand, you can handle the `page.on('filechooser')` event or use a corresponding waiting method upon your action.

For example, you can start waiting for the file chooser before clicking the button:

```javascript
// Start waiting for file chooser before clicking. Note no await.
const fileChooserPromise = page.waitForEvent('filechooser');
await page.getByLabel('Upload file').click();
const fileChooser = await fileChooserPromise;
await fileChooser.setFiles(path.join(__dirname, 'myfile.pdf'));
```

